{"type":"agent_end","messages":[{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Read prompt.md and complete the exercise following the workflow rules. Continue autonomously through ALL tests in the test list until you have written experiment-done.txt with the single word DONE. Do NOT stop after a single passing test or cycle — keep going until every test is implemented."}],"timestamp":1784969498140},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Let me start by reading the prompt.md file to understand what exercise I need to complete.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_0b1ef2276099405e8692621b","name":"read","arguments":{"path":"prompt.md"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"requesty","model":"tensorx/glm-5.2","usage":{"input":3220,"output":30,"cacheRead":1792,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":19,"totalTokens":5042,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1784969498180,"responseId":"rqsty-cmpl-b860403d-6cd5-4a85-b949-42e78541253e","responseModel":"z-ai/glm-5.2"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_0b1ef2276099405e8692621b","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"# Game of Life Kata - Experiment Prompt\n\n## Input\n\nImplement Conway's Game of Life with an **infinite grid** (theoretically unlimited cells in all x and y directions).\n\n## Feature: Game of Life - Next Generation\n\n### Rules\n\n1. **Underpopulation**: Any live cell with fewer than 2 live neighbors dies\n2. **Survival**: Any live cell with 2 or 3 live neighbors lives on\n3. **Overpopulation**: Any live cell with more than 3 live neighbors dies\n4. **Reproduction**: Any dead cell with exactly 3 live neighbors becomes alive\n\n### Constraints\n\n- Grid is **infinite** in all directions (positive and negative x/y)\n- Only track **living cells** (sparse representation)\n- Cells are identified by coordinates `(x, y)`\n- A \"generation\" transforms the current state to the next state\n\n### Examples\n\n#### Examples per Rule\n\n**Rule 1 – Underpopulation** (live cell with < 2 neighbors dies):\n```\nGen 0:       Gen 1:\n ##           ..\n ..     →     ..\n```\nCoordinates Gen 0: `[(0,1), (1,1)]` (each has 1 neighbor)\nCoordinates Gen 1: `[]`\n\n**Rule 2 – Survival** (live cell with 2 or 3 neighbors lives on):\n```\nGen 0:       Gen 1:\n ###          .#.\n ...    →     .#.\n .#.          ...\n```\nThe center cell `(1,1)` has 3 live neighbors → survives.\n\n**Rule 3 – Overpopulation** (live cell with > 3 neighbors dies):\n```\nGen 0:       Gen 1:\n ###          #.#\n .#.    →     #.#\n ###          #.#\n```\nCenter cell `(1,1)` has 4 live neighbors → dies.\n\n**Rule 4 – Reproduction** (dead cell with exactly 3 neighbors becomes alive):\n```\nGen 0:       Gen 1:\n ##.          ##.\n #..    →     ##.\n ...          ...\n```\nDead cell `(1,1)` has exactly 3 live neighbors → becomes alive.\n\n#### Pattern Examples\n\n**Blinker (oscillator)**:\n```\nGen 0:       Gen 1:       Gen 2:\n  .#.          ...          .#.\n  .#.    →     ###    →     .#.\n  .#.          ...          .#.\n```\nCoordinates Gen 0: `[(0,0), (0,1), (0,2)]`\nCoordinates Gen 1: `[(-1,1), (0,1), (1,1)]`\n\n**Block (still life)**:\n```\nGen 0:       Gen 1:\n  ##           ##\n  ##     →     ##\n```\nCoordinates: `[(0,0), (1,0), (0,1), (1,1)]` → unchanged\n\n**Single cell dies**:\n```\nGen 0:       Gen 1:\n  #      →     .\n```\nCoordinates Gen 0: `[(0,0)]`\nCoordinates Gen 1: `[]` (empty)\n\n## Task\n\nImplement the Game of Life based on the rules and examples above.\n\nThe implementation should accept an arbitrary grid of living cells and output the next generation.\n\n## API contract\n\nExport from `src/game-of-life.ts` a function with this signature:\n\n```ts\ntype Cell = [number, number]; // [x, y]\nexport function nextGeneration(cells: Cell[]): Cell[];\n```\n\nInput and output are arrays of `[x, y]` coordinate tuples (matching the coordinate notation used in the examples above). Internally you may use whatever data structure suits you (Set, Map, …), but the function boundary must match the signature above.\n\n## Expected Output Files\n\n- `src/game-of-life.ts` - Implementation\n- `src/game-of-life.spec.ts` - Tests\n\n## Constraints\n\n- Use TypeScript\n- Use sparse representation (only store living cells)\n- Handle negative coordinates\n\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1784969499350},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now I understand the task. Let me explore the project structure to understand what's already there.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_06f7a09074c2460eb3a5da01","name":"bash","arguments":{"command":"cd /home/experimenter/experiments/runs/2026-07-25_08-51-36_game-of-life-example-mapping_v6.2.1-phase-continuation-pi_glm-5-2 && ls -la && echo \"---SRC---\" && ls -la src/ 2>/dev/null || echo \"no src dir\" && echo \"---PI---\" && ls -la .pi/ 2>/dev/null"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"requesty","model":"tensorx/glm-5.2","usage":{"input":900,"output":123,"cacheRead":4992,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":20,"totalTokens":6015,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1784969499351,"responseId":"rqsty-cmpl-275119eb-1c64-4b44-8616-6c0c0c82c57d","responseModel":"z-ai/glm-5.2"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_06f7a09074c2460eb3a5da01","toolName":"bash","content":[{"type":"text","text":"total 408\ndrwxr-xr-x    5 experimenter experimenter   4096 Jul 25 08:51 .\ndrwxrwxr-x 1043 experimenter experimenter 163840 Jul 25 08:51 ..\ndrwxr-xr-x    5 experimenter experimenter   4096 Jul 25 08:51 .pi\n-rw-r--r--    1 experimenter experimenter  11746 Jul 25 08:51 AGENTS.md\n-rw-r--r--    1 experimenter experimenter   1568 Jul 25 08:51 eslint.config.mjs\n-rw-r--r--    1 experimenter experimenter    372 Jul 25 08:51 metrics.json\ndrwxr-xr-x    3 experimenter experimenter   4096 Jul 25 08:51 node_modules\n-rw-